<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Second Taifa of Niebla</h1><p class="st-meta">1145 CE – 1150 CE (approx.) · capital Niebla</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Niebla's brief independence under Yusuf al-Bitruji during the 1140s revolts against the Almoravids in the far west of al-Andalus.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1145 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-ibn-ahmad-al-bitruji">Yusuf ibn Ahmad al-Bitruji</a>, a local leader, took control of the walled town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niebla">Niebla</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-tinto">Tinto</a> river, as the revolt begun by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-qasi">Ibn Qasi</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algarve">Algarve</a> spread through the south-west.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Known only from brief chronicle references, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niebla">Niebla</a> was one of several small regimes that rose and fell in quick succession. Its ruler was drawn into conflicts with Almoravid loyalists in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a> and with neighbouring rebels.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niebla">Niebla</a> submitted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a> around 1150. A century later it became independent again as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/third-taifa-of-niebla">Third Taifa of Niebla</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1145 CE – 1150 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:82.49%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1145 CE – 1150 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Niebla</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Yusuf ibn Ahmad al-Bitruji</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Andalusi Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Niebla of Yusuf ibn Ahmad al-Bitruji</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1148&amp;focus=second-taifa-of-niebla" aria-label="Second Taifa of Niebla on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4513 833 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Second Taifa of Niebla lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4833 1089L4799 1289M4833 1089L4794 1282"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4799 1289h0M4794 1282h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4833 1089h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4833 1089h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Niebla. <a href="/atlas?year=1148&amp;focus=second-taifa-of-niebla">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
